1
00:00:00,442 --> 00:00:06,656
Azhi Flow: governed, durable agent workflows that say plainly what they can and cannot guarantee.

2
00:00:06,656 --> 00:00:09,739
Agents die halfway.

3
00:00:09,739 --> 00:00:12,826
Retries post twice.

4
00:00:12,826 --> 00:00:16,990
Nobody can say what it cost, or what it was allowed to do.

5
00:00:16,990 --> 00:00:21,495
Azhi starts from the workflow, not the agent.

6
00:00:21,495 --> 00:00:25,819
One screen for what is running, what needs you, and what it cost.

7
00:00:25,819 --> 00:00:29,822
Spend is measured, never guessed.

8
00:00:29,822 --> 00:00:36,297
Risky steps wait for a person.

9
00:00:36,522 --> 00:00:39,358
A workflow of nodes. An agent is just one kind.

10
00:00:39,358 --> 00:00:43,114
Only these five steps call a model.

11
00:00:43,114 --> 00:00:48,866
Fetch, route, report and post are plain code: zero tokens.

12
00:00:48,866 --> 00:00:55,341
Select a step to read what it does and every setting.

13
00:00:55,395 --> 00:00:59,923
Edit on the canvas. The server compiles and plans every change.

14
00:00:59,923 --> 00:01:06,398
Per-agent harness: executor, prompt, skills, read-only tools, MCP server and budget.

15
00:01:11,575 --> 00:01:17,829
Add a step from the palette. Tools come from the catalog.

16
00:01:17,829 --> 00:01:24,304
Taint rule: a write after an agent that read untrusted code will not compile without a guard.

17
00:01:29,535 --> 00:01:36,010
Pin the write to the reviewed pull request. It compiles with no blockers.

18
00:01:38,559 --> 00:01:42,416
What it saw, what it was allowed to do, what it did, and what it cost.

19
00:01:42,416 --> 00:01:48,891
Replay the run, step by step.

20
00:01:51,893 --> 00:01:58,203
Action ledger: every external write with receipts. Exactly once, even after a crash.

21
00:01:58,203 --> 00:02:04,488
Policy coverage: what Azhi enforces itself, and what it only trusts the harness for.

22
00:02:04,488 --> 00:02:10,852
Context manifest: every source the model saw, with hashes. Untrusted data is flagged.

23
00:02:10,852 --> 00:02:17,327
Cost per step: nine model calls, thirty-one cents, usage known for one hundred percent.

24
00:02:17,808 --> 00:02:24,283
Approvals carry the payload and who may decide. The decision is kept in the ledger.

25
00:02:27,003 --> 00:02:32,189
Spend per day and per workflow: tokens in, tokens out and dollars.

26
00:02:32,189 --> 00:02:36,940
Spend limits per workflow, per day or month. At the limit new runs are refused.

27
00:02:36,940 --> 00:02:40,185
Unpriced turns show as unknown, never as zero.

28
00:02:40,185 --> 00:02:46,660
How Azhi saves tokens: no model for steps that do not need one, projected tool output, top_k retrieval, per-step budgets, heavy harness only where needed, and prompt caching.

29
00:02:53,208 --> 00:02:59,683
What Azhi does that agent runners do not: run plan, taint gate, exactly-once writes, context manifest, durable runs, and your choice of harness with signed packages.

30
00:03:07,849 --> 00:03:14,324
Try it: azhi init, azhi up. Self-hosted. github.com/surr-jc/azhi-flow
